From: Isaac Connor <connortechnology@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] vf_drawtext_ni: add an update command that does not close
 the scaler sessions

Against Quadra V5.8.0 (libxcoder 5806tCr2).

Changing the text on this filter costs two hardware session teardowns and
two frame pool reallocations per frame, because "reinit" is the only way
to do it.

command() builds a fresh NetIntDrawTextContext, av_opt_copy()s the
options across and uninit()s the old one. session_opened and
crop_session_opened are plain fields rather than AVOptions, so they are
not copied: they start at zero in the new context, while uninit() closes
the two scaler sessions the old one held. The next filter_frame reopens
both and rebuilds both pools.

On a 3840x2160 h264 stream labelling detections, changing the label 6 to
12 times a second, that churn starves the card:

  drawtext blocked 6.37s on 2 labels (4 of 11 calls)
  send_packet avg 96.3ms exceeds frame budget 66.5ms (capture 15fps)

drawtext went back to spinning in ni_scaler_session_read_hwdesc for
seconds at a time -- the same starvation patch 1 of this series fixes --
and the decoder stopped making its frame budget, so frames were dropped
and went out unannotated. Measured cost was 45ms a call against 7ms for
the draw alone.

None of what a caller changes per frame needs the session rebuilt.
text_num is counted from which slots carry text, x and y are evaluated
from x_pexpr/y_pexpr rather than the option strings, and a slot used for
the first time needs its face, size and glyphs. fontsize already
re-parses itself in update_fontsize() on every frame.

Add an "update" command that applies the option string to the live
context and re-derives exactly those, leaving the sessions and the pools
alone. "reinit" keeps its meaning for callers that want a full rebuild.

Depends on patch 2 of this series: without AV_OPT_FLAG_RUNTIME_PARAM the
av_set_options_string() here is refused the same way reinit's was.

--- a/libavfilter/vf_drawtext_ni.c
+++ b/libavfilter/vf_drawtext_ni.c
@@ -1632,6 +1632,85 @@
     NetIntDrawTextContext *new = NULL;
     int ret;
 
+    /* Set the per-frame options on the live context and re-derive only what
+     * they feed. reinit cannot be used for this on a hardware filter: it
+     * builds a fresh context whose session_opened and crop_session_opened
+     * start at zero -- they are plain fields, not AVOptions, so av_opt_copy
+     * does not carry them -- and then uninit()s the old one, closing both
+     * scaler sessions. The next frame reopens them and rebuilds both frame
+     * pools. Per frame that is two session teardowns and two pool
+     * reallocations, which starves the card: measured on a 3840x2160 stream
+     * at 6 to 12 label changes a second, drawtext went back to blocking for
+     * seconds at a time in ni_scaler_session_read_hwdesc and the decoder
+     * stopped making its frame budget.
+     *
+     * Nothing a label needs touches the session. text_num is counted from
+     * which slots carry text, x and y are evaluated from parsed expressions
+     * rather than the option strings, and a slot used for the first time
+     * needs its face and glyphs. Do those and leave the hardware alone.
+     */
+    if (!strcmp(cmd, "update")) {
+        NetIntDrawTextContext *s = ctx->priv;
+        int old_text_num = s->text_num;
+        Glyph *glyph;
+        int i;
+
+        ret = av_set_options_string(ctx, arg, "=", ":");
+        if (ret < 0)
+            return ret;
+
+        s->text_num = 0;
+        for (i = 0; i < MAX_TEXT_NUM; i++) {
+            if (!s->text[i])
+                break;
+            s->text_num++;
+        }
+        if (!s->text_num) {
+            av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "update needs at least one text\n");
+            s->text_num = old_text_num;
+            return AVERROR(EINVAL);
+        }
+
+        for (i = old_text_num; i < s->text_num; i++) {
+            if ((ret = load_font(ctx, i)) < 0)
+                return ret;
+            if ((ret = update_fontsize(ctx, i)) < 0)
+                return ret;
+            s->use_kerning[i] = FT_HAS_KERNING(s->face[i]);
+            /* the fallback glyph, as init() does */
+            load_glyph(ctx, NULL, 0, i);
+            if ((ret = load_glyph(ctx, &glyph, ' ', i)) < 0) {
+                av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Could not set tabsize.\n");
+                return ret;
+            }
+            /* tabsize[0] is already in pixels by the time init() is done with
+             * it, so take it as it stands rather than scaling it again.
+             */
+            s->tabsize[i] = s->tabsize[0];
+        }
+
+        for (i = 0; i < s->text_num; i++) {
+            const char *expr;
+
+            av_expr_free(s->x_pexpr[i]);
+            av_expr_free(s->y_pexpr[i]);
+            s->x_pexpr[i] = s->y_pexpr[i] = NULL;
+
+            if ((ret = av_expr_parse(&s->x_pexpr[i], expr = s->x_expr[i],
+                                     var_names, NULL, NULL, fun2_names, fun2,
+                                     0, ctx)) < 0 ||
+                (ret = av_expr_parse(&s->y_pexpr[i], expr = s->y_expr[i],
+                                     var_names, NULL, NULL, fun2_names, fun2,
+                                     0, ctx)) < 0) {
+                av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Failed to parse expression: %s\n", expr);
+                return AVERROR(EINVAL);
+            }
+        }
+
+        /* fontsize is re-parsed by update_fontsize() on every frame already */
+        return 0;
+    }
+
     if (!strcmp(cmd, "reinit")) {
         new = av_mallocz(sizeof(NetIntDrawTextContext));
         if (!new)
